OPL GUIDES


BIGREF.DOC
==========
This is a summary of the OPL keywords, their syntax, and explanations of
how they work. Joe and I hacked it out of Chapter 13 of the Series 3
Programming Manual. I think it's correct - it's even had a few bugfixes
which the manual may not have - but since it's a bit on the `quick+dirty'
side, the layout of each record/entry may not be ideal.

The weird characters in this file (ASCII 21) are forced linebreaks.

If you want to carry this around as a database on your Series 3:

*) Make a new, empty database

*) Select the `Merge in' option. Set the filename, then set the 
`Merge in' line to `Text' and `Delimiter' to `Newline'. Press Enter.

To find the description of a particular keyword, search for it with
a dot before the name (e.g.     .glineby   ).

You may find any or all of these tips useful:

*) Either use `Hide labels', or edit them. Only the first three 
lines/fields can be labelled in any sensible way; you may like to 
use `Name:', `Usage:' and `Notes:', or something similar.

*) Set `Wrap on'.

*) Increase the `Tab spacing' from 4 to 6, or even 8. (I think...)

*) Get rid of the Status Window, with Control-Menu.


SMALLREF.DOC
============
This is a summary of the OPL keywords and the syntax to use with them.
It is in the same format as BIGREF.DOC - merge it in as a text file, 
with `Newline' as the delimiter.

`Hide labels', `Wrap on' and Control-Menu may again be useful.
No labels should be applied, and there are no tabs in this file.




Please distribute freely. Comments are welcome.
